VMware Workstation Pro or Player installed (version 17.x or later).
ISO files:
Kali Linux: kali-linux-2023.4-vmware-amd64.7z or newer.
Ubuntu: ubuntu-24.04-desktop-amd64.iso or equivalent.
Minimum system resources:
16 GB RAM (8 GB per VM recommended).
50+ GB free disk space.
4+ CPU cores.
Step-by-step instructions
Install VMware Workstation
Download from VMware’s official site or use terminal:
wget https://download3.vmware.com/software/WKST-1750-LX/VMware-Workstation-Full-17.5.0-22583795.x86_64.bundle
chmod +x VMware-Workstation-Full-*.bundle
sudo ./VMware-Workstation-Full-*.bundle

Create a New Virtual Machine
Open VMware → File → New Virtual Machine → Choose "Typical" → Select "Installer disc image file (iso)" → Browse and select your Kali or Ubuntu ISO. 
Set Guest OS Type
For Kali: Select Linux → Debian 12.x 64-bit.
For Ubuntu: Select Linux → Ubuntu 64-bit. 
Name and Location
Set VM name (e.g., Kali-Pentest, Ubuntu-Dev) and choose storage path. 
Disk Capacity
Allocate at least 30 GB for Kali, 40 GB for Ubuntu.  Choose "Store as a single file".
Customize Hardware (Optional)
Increase RAM to 4–8 GB, CPUs to 2–4 cores, and add a network adapter (Bridged or NAT). 
Finish and Power On
Click Finish → Power on the VM to start OS installation. 
Install the OS
Follow on-screen steps:
For Kali: Default credentials are kali/kali.
For Ubuntu: Create your user and password. 
Install VMware Tools (Open VM Tools)
After OS install:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install open-vm-tools open-vm-tools-desktop -y

Reboot the VM.
Enable Shared Folders
In VMware:
Go to VM → Settings → Options → Shared Folders → Enable and add host folder.
In guest (Linux), mount using:
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/hgfs
sudo vmhgfs-fuse .host:/ /mnt/hgfs -o allow_other

Auto-mount at boot: Add to /etc/fstab:
.host:/ /mnt/hgfs fuse.vmhgfs-fuse defaults,allow_other 0 0

Post-Setup Updates
Update both systems:
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

Secure Boot (if on Linux host)
If modules fail, sign vmmon and vmnet:
openssl req -new -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout VMWARE.priv -outform DER -out VMWARE.der -nodes -days 36500 -subj "/CN=VMWARE/"
sudo /usr/src/linux-headers-$(uname -r)/scripts/sign-file sha256 ./VMWARE.priv ./VMWARE.der $(modinfo -n vmmon)
sudo /usr/src/linux-headers-$(uname -r)/scripts/sign-file sha256 ./VMWARE.priv ./VMWARE.der $(modinfo -n vmnet)
sudo mokutil --import VMWARE.der
